{
  "mn140:0.1": "Middle Discourses 140 ",
  "mn140:0.2": "The Analysis of the Elements ",
  "mn140:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn140:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was wandering in the Magadhan lands when he arrived at Rājagaha. ",
  "mn140:1.3": "He went to see Bhaggava the potter, and said, ",
  "mn140:2.1": "“Bhaggava, if it is no trouble, I’d like to spend a single night in your workshop.” ",
  "mn140:2.2": "“It’s no trouble, sir. ",
  "mn140:2.3": "But there’s a renunciate already staying there. ",
  "mn140:2.4": "If he allows it, sir, you may stay as long as you please.” ",
  "mn140:3.1": "Now at that time a gentleman named Pukkusāti had gone forth out of faith from the lay life to homelessness in the Buddha’s name. ",
  "mn140:3.2": "And it was he who had first taken up residence in the workshop. ",
  "mn140:3.3": "Then the Buddha approached Venerable Pukkusāti and said, ",
  "mn140:3.4": "“Mendicant, if it is no trouble, I’d like to spend a single night in the workshop.” ",
  "mn140:3.5": "“The potter’s workshop is spacious, reverend. ",
  "mn140:3.6": "Stay as long as you please.” ",
  "mn140:4.1": "Then the Buddha entered the workshop and spread out a grass mat to one side. He sat down cross-legged, set his body straight, and brought mindfulness to the present. ",
  "mn140:4.2": "He spent much of the night sitting in meditation, ",
  "mn140:4.3": "and so did Pukkusāti. ",
  "mn140:4.4": "Then it occurred to the Buddha, ",
